        "title": "macOS 27 adds new Apple Intelligence features to your favorite apps",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/25/macos-27-adds-new-apple-intelligence-features-to-your-favorite-apps/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/apple-intelligence.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>9to5Mac is brought to you by <a href=\"https://bit.ly/3V7JCmu\">CleanMyMac by MacPaw</a>. With the release of macOS 27 Golden Gate, use CleanMyMac first to free up space, optimize your system, and ensure your new Mac runs at 100% on day one. <a href=\"https://bit.ly/3V7JCmu\">Learn more</a>.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/14/macos-27-golden-gate-now-available-here-is-everything-new/\">released macOS 27 Golden Gate</a> to the public after several months of beta testing. The update is headlined by Siri AI, but there are also Apple Intelligence enhancements to many of Apple’s own Mac apps. Here are a few of my favorites.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1070528\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/25/macos-27-adds-new-apple-intelligence-features-to-your-favorite-apps/#more-1070528\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
