        "content_text": "Manchester City are the most successful (men's) football team in the modern era of the Premier League. But there's a slight problem. <a href=\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/c65y51l3gzq4o\">They cheated</a>, to the sum of <a href=\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/c9lyk46gekkeo\">&#0163;830,690,000</a>. For 9 seasons, during which they <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/sep/29/manchester-city-sham-seasons-how-they-fared-and-who-was-in-charge\">won a number of titles and trophies</a>. After a multi-year investigation, <a href=\"https://www.premierleague.com/en/news/4727779/premier-league-statement-manchester-city-fc\">further details</a>.",
