        "title": "Instagram partner schools can now post content only their students can view",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/29/instagram-partner-schools-can-now-post-content-only-their-students-can-view/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/Instagram-partner-schools-can-now-post-content-only-their-students-can-view.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/meta/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Meta</a> last year launched a school partnership program for <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/instagram/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a>, in which it promised to prioritize student reports of cyberbullying.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The company has now expanded the program to allow schools to post stories and notes that only their own students can view – alongside support for clubs, teams, and more …</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apps,instagram\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1071880\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/29/instagram-partner-schools-can-now-post-content-only-their-students-can-view/#more-1071880\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
