        "url": "https://9to5google.com/2026/09/29/google-firebase-iphone-app-crash-fixed/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/iPhone-18-Pro-homescreen.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">An issue with Google’s Firebase left thousands of iPhone apps crashing overnight, but a fix has already been applied.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"firebase,ios\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1071881\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/09/29/google-firebase-iphone-app-crash-fixed/#more-1071881\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
