        "url": "https://www.oreilly.com/radar/from-raw-data-to-graph-native-ai/",
        "content_text": "I’ve been thinking about a gap in the way we discuss graphs in AI. Most of the conversation starts after the graph already exists. We talk about graph neural networks, GraphRAG, graph agents, and graph foundation models. We spend much less time on the step that determines what all of them can do: turning raw [&#8230;]",
