        "title": "Search for the answers",
        "url": "https://www.metafilter.com/214678/Search-for-the-answers",
        "content_text": "<a href=\"https://www.gamemeca.com/en/view.php?gid=1780605\">Database thrillers</a> are a subgenre of <a href=\"https://azhdarchid.com/against-metroidbrania-a-landscape-of-knowledge-games/\">knowledge games/thinky games/metroidbranias</a> where the primary mechanic involves searching through databases and other sources for information to solve a mystery. Tumblr user velteris has complied <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/velteris/828278995121487872/so-this-popped-off-and-im-glad-that-theres-been?source=share\">an extensive list of database thrillers and similar games</a>, including <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2754380/The_Roottrees_are_Dead/\">The Roottrees Are Dead</a>, <a href=\"https://william-rous.itch.io/type-help\">Type Help</a> (recently remastered as <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3641000/The_Incident_at_Galley_House/\">The Incident at Galley House</a>), and <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/368370/Her_Story/\">Her Story</a>. <small>(note: the first link is originally in Korean but translated by the website itself into English using AI)</small>",
