        "url": "https://www.oreilly.com/radar/ai-sovereignty-bargaining-with-big-tech-and-the-promise-of-full-stack-open-source-ai/",
        "content_text": "The early rapid expansion of AI capabilities that focused on frontier models was largely ushered into the world by a few powerful, US-based AI labs. Open-weight models released from labs in China, early on from DeepSeek, and later from Moonshot, Z.ai, and others, have in part disrupted that dominance. But growing concerns about the concentration [&#8230;]",
